sentences.l:
At once, for the one, then, over his eyes he poured a haze,
for Peleus’-son Achilles; and he the ash-spear of good bronze
out of the shield of great-spirited Aeneas drew;

sentences.t:
Αἰνεία, τίς σ’ ὧδε θεῶν ἀτέοντα κελεύει
ἀντία Πηλεΐωνος ὑπερθύμοιο μάχεσθαι,
ὃς σεῦ ἅμα κρείσσων καὶ φίλτερος ἀθανάτοισιν;

sentences.tr:
Aineia, tis s’ hōde theōn ateonta keleuei
antia Pēleïōnos hyperthymoio machesthai,
hos seu hama kreissōn kai philteros athanatoisin;

sentences.l:
And not the bronze helmet held, but through it
the spear-point, driving on, broke the bone, and the brain
within all was spattered;

But he gasped out his life and bellowed, as when a bull
bellows, dragged about the Heliconian lord
by youths who drag him; and the earth-shaker is delighted with them;

and dearest to him he was, and in his feet he beat them all;
so then, in childish ways showing the excellence of his feet,
he rushed through the front-fighters, until he lost his dear life.

Him struck in the middle with a javelin swift-footed, heavenly Achilles,
on the back as he darted past, where of the belt the clasps
golden held together and the double breastplate met them;
